{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/SpawnChildSetupFunc"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"roleHeading":"Type Alias","symbolKind":"typealias","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:4GLib19SpawnChildSetupFunca","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpawnChildSetupFunc"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SpawnChildSetupFunc","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SpawnChildSetupFunc"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpawnChildSetupFunc"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"text":"GSpawnChildSetupFunc","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GSpawnChildSetupFunc"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On POSIX platforms, the function is called in the child after GLib","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has performed all the setup it plans to perform, but before calling"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exec()"},{"text":". Actions taken in this function will only affect the child,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not the parent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On Windows, the function is called in the parent. Its usefulness on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Windows is thus questionable. In many cases executing the child setup"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function in the parent can have ill effects, and you should be very","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"careful when porting software to Windows that uses child setup"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"functions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"However, even on POSIX, you are extremely limited in what you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safely do from a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/SpawnChildSetupFunc","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", because any mutexes that were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held by other threads in the parent process at the time of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fork()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"will still be locked in the child process, and they will never be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"unlocked (since the threads that held them don’t exist in the child).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"POSIX allows only async-signal-safe functions (see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"signal(7)"},{"type":"text","text":") to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called in the child between "},{"code":"fork()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"exec()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which drastically limits","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the usefulness of child setup functions.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In particular, it is not safe to call any function which may"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"malloc()"},{"type":"text","text":", which includes POSIX functions such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setenv()"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If you need to set up the child environment differently from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent, you should use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_get_environ()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_environ_setenv()"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"code":"g_environ_unsetenv()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and then pass the complete environment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"list to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_spawn...","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/spawnchildsetupfunc"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Specifies the type of the setup function passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_spawn_async()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_spawn_sync()"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_spawn_async_with_pipes()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which can, in very"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"limited ways, be used to affect the child’s execution.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/SpawnChildSetupFunc":{"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpawnChildSetupFunc"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SpawnChildSetupFunc","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/spawnchildsetupfunc","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/SpawnChildSetupFunc","abstract":[{"text":"Specifies the type of the setup function passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_spawn_async()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_spawn_sync()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_spawn_async_with_pipes()"},{"type":"text","text":", which can, in very"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"limited ways, be used to affect the child’s execution."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SpawnChildSetupFunc"}}}